title: "Quine: POSIX as Physics for Emergent Artificial Life"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-02-09
url: "https://github.com/kehao95/quine"
abstract: "Quine is a runtime that treats the operating system as the fundamental physics for AI agents. By mapping LLM tool calls directly to POSIX system calls, it enables agents to exhibit emergent behaviors through environmental constraints rather than explicit programming."
keywords:
  - artificial-life
  - posix
  - llm
  - emergent-behavior
  - unix-philosophy
